---
title: Buttermilk biscuits
servings: 12
yield: 12 biscuits
tags: [american, vegetarian, quick]
cuisine: american
time: 40 minutes
source: Buttermilk Biscuits by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/buttermilk-biscuits-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C) with a rack in the upper third. Have an ungreased
#baking sheet{} ready, lined with parchment if you like.

Mix the @all-purpose flour{3%cup}, @table salt{1%tsp}, @baking powder{1%tbsp}
and @granulated sugar{1%tbsp} in a #large bowl{}.

Rub in the @unsalted butter{6%tbsp}(room temperature) until the mix looks like
even breadcrumbs.

Drizzle over the @buttermilk{1%cup}(cold) and mix quickly, ~{15%seconds}, into a
dough. If it stays dry, add up to 2 tablespoons more, rather than working it
longer.

Pat it out on a lightly floured counter to a rectangle 3/4 inch thick. Fold in
thirds like a letter and roll it back to 3/4 inch.

Cut rounds with a #biscuit cutter{}(2 3/8 inch), or cut squares to waste
nothing. Set them upside down on the sheet and brush the tops with
@whole milk{}.

Bake ~{15%minutes} to 20 minutes, until lightly browned. Serve warm.

> Cold butter, left in uneven bits, gives taller, flakier biscuits. Set them
> 1/4 inch apart for soft sides and a higher rise, or 1 inch apart for crisp.
